<description>&lt;p&gt;Ecuador is enforcing a fourth curfew through Nov. 10 in five coastal provinces as violence escalates, and the military has begun its first land operation against cartels with U.S. assistance, including U.S. Marines seizing a vessel linked to the Los Choneros gang in the eastern Pacific. Heavy rain on Santa Cruz Island in the Galapagos killed one person and left two missing, and a priest was killed when a crucifix fell on him, prompting an archbishop to announce a clergy safety plan. President Daniel Noboa continues to detain opposition leader Luisa González on money-laundering charges. The crisis recorded two battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuwFBVV95cUxQNWZ6Mk5ESjdOZmxod2xqV1FTWmUyck13RXM0YnFWTzJPTi1PcG42OXpqTVAtVWhPbkU1VEVVbTVnTEdiRUIxeVJ1aFlJZ29JckhjdXJRMmp1VVgwN0RjTElhdU9NSGVuUVJubGx1bzlCM3BfczdBVTZJTmtSM243VmNCZFVxVk9ZVEl4Sm5PbWNkMXNPMVo3WDVFZkJDdHVQcjV1X085aXllNkRwWWNmQXB2ZlNUQ2o1STNz?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eurasia Review&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Weekly Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxOQWhQZ0owZVB3TmJCRUYwdDBwWmtBLVp5S0ZDTW1LRGNpRVZjeEJ1S21qM0xjLVFVR3Y2SmMtc3hoUHMtMTczbUFTTF9zZ2hjdUtTT05oYUZnMDY4bjByeVpldDd5OUJERC1uSmg5aEdVU0FFNW91V2xsOHlmLXlKVTY2WWszcUZSMmpXajZ1cw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Latin Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE1oSjZSanBySnBpLU1KRGJlcTR2dHdqeDZIb213NEZHRUhKa3VPY3RIM202aU5KZG12a1RxYVAyMHZnNDJMaUNPOEdGLWNjUWhiOFZ4VlQ3SEt6YW9QUWh5T0VhQXFWbmVQU3prd2FsZ3ZsVk1ySmJB?oc=5&quot;&gt;Nhan Dan Online&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiaEFVX3lxTE1tQ2RpT3pjTzJoMHlXN0lMVGRTZ1R4aW9qTlRxRExQcHEwc2s0YXdWdHlnd0d4OWgyYjBkZjhlQXZnb19vT3JUZktqS2NzcWctRWcyS1JzSWFfeHZwTjVaOE9